{'query': 'reputable peer-reviewed scientific source on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': '(PDF) Understanding Climate Change: A Review of Causes ...', 'url': 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397706496_Understanding_Climate_Change_A_Review_of_Causes_Impacts_and_Responses', 'snippet': 'Nov 18, 2025 · This brief summarizes and analyzes the natural and human causes of the greenhouse effect, the existing scientific evidence, and the environmental, economic, and social impacts of climate...'}, {'title': 'A review of the global climate change impacts, adaptation ...', 'url': 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8978769/', 'snippet': 'This review aims to highlight the effects of climate change in a socio-scientific aspect by analyzing the existing literature on various sectorial pieces of evidence globally that influence the environment.'}, {'title': 'Climate change and its environmental and health effects from ...', 'url': 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405844025006954', 'snippet': 'Feb 15, 2025 · This review seeks to investigate the far-reaching effects of climate change on health and the associated environmental consequences, both on a global scale and within the EMRO region.'}, {'title': 'Science of climate change', 'url': 'https://scienceofclimatechange.org/', 'snippet': 'Science of Climate Change (SCC) is an independent, peer-reviewed, open-access scholarly journal dedicated to advancing scientific understanding of the Earth’s climate system and its governing processes.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change - Recent articles and discoveries - Springer', 'url': 'https://link.springer.com/subjects/climate-change', 'snippet': '1 day ago · Uncover the latest and most impactful research in Climate Change. Explore pioneering discoveries, insightful ideas and new methods from leading researchers in the field.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 3.178639199992176}
{'query': 'government or international body report on global average temperatures and climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate change: global temperature | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-global-temperature', 'snippet': 'Climate change: global temperature. By Rebecca Lindsey AND LuAnn Dahlman Reviewed by Jessica Blunden.Past and future change in global temperature. Temperature change has not been uniform across the planet, but more areas are warming than cooling.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/global-issues/climate-change', 'snippet': 'Climate change refers to long-term shifts in temperatures and weather patterns. Although some climate variations occur naturally, human activities have been the main driver of climate change since the 1800s, mainly through the burning of fossil fuels such as coal, oil, and gas.'}, {'title': "Page 7 of 1866 - The world's most viewed site on global warming and...", 'url': 'https://wattsupwiththat.com/page/7/', 'snippet': 'Geomagnetism Page. Global Temperature – Climate.The report argues that protecting endangered species remains a worthy objective, but that the ESA’s implementation needs significant reform to better respect property rights, sound science and responsible government.'}, {'title': 'Global warming | Definition, Causes, Effects, Solutions... | Britannica', 'url': 'https://www.britannica.com/science/global-warming', 'snippet': 'In addition to changes in air temperature, climate change involves changes to precipitation patterns, winds, ocean currents, and other measures of Earth’s climate. Normally, climate change can be viewed as the combination of various natural forces occurring over diverse timescales.'}, {'title': 'NASA is a global leader in studying Earth’s changing climate.', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'What is causing climate change? Human activities are driving the global warming trend observed since the mid-20th century.Scientists predict global temperature increases from human-made greenhouse gases will continue. Severe weather damage will also increase and intensify.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 4.354681199998595}
{'query': 'recent news claim global average temperatures started decreasing 2023-2024 and verification from scientific sources', 'results': [{'title': 'Temperatures Rising: NASA Confirms 2024 Warmest Year on... - NASA', 'url': 'https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/temperatures-rising-nasa-confirms-2024-warmest-year-on-record/', 'snippet': 'This map of Earth in 2024 shows global surface temperature anomalies, or how much warmer or cooler each region of the planet was compared to the average from 1951 to 1980.'}, {'title': 'Climate change: global temperature | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-global-temperature', 'snippet': 'Global temperatures in 2024 were above the 1991-2020 average (red) across most of the planet. Yearly temperatures compared to the 20th-century average (bar chart) show that it has been 48 years since Earth had a cooler-than-average year.'}, {'title': 'Interactive temperature map. Shows global forecasted temperatures.', 'url': 'https://zoom.earth/maps/temperature/', 'snippet': 'Heat spots are not live! Detections are updated daily and are delayed by many hours. Red spots show the approximate locations of very high temperature detected by satellite. These spots may be from fire or other sources of heat such as hot smoke or agriculture.'}, {'title': 'February 2024 and Winter 2023-2024 Climate Summaries', 'url': 'https://www.weather.gov/lot/February_2024_Winter_2023-2024_Climate_Summaries', 'snippet': 'Weather.gov > Chicago, IL > February 2024 and Winter 2023-2024 Climate Summaries.The average temperature for the month was 39.5 degrees, which is 10.7 degrees above normal. 0.65 inches of liquid precipitation were recorded, which is 1.32 inches below normal.'}, {'title': 'Trends in CO2 - NOAA Global Monitoring Laboratory', 'url': 'https://gml.noaa.gov/ccgg/trends/', 'snippet': 'Monthly Average Mauna Loa CO2.NOAA started its own CO2 measurements in May of 1974, and they have run in parallel with those made by Scripps since then [Thoning, 1989].'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 3.687751300021773}
